  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Motor Oil Hellas Corinth Refineries S A has federal contract obligations of $723M in FY2026 to date. The company received 28 awards so far, with an average award size of $25.8M, and obligations are up 31.1% year over year. Petroleum Refineries is the dominant NAICS market with $723M in obligations, while Other Warehousing and Storage accounts for $148K. Obligations have varied across recent fiscal years: FY21 was $181M, FY22 was $560M, FY23 was $272M, FY24 was $530M, FY25 was $551M, and FY26 is $723M. The current-year totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date contract obligations. The mix of award counts, large average award size, and a single dominant market indicates concentrated federal spending on refinery-related work. Readers should note that the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables show total contract values rather than current-year obligations, and that FY2026 figures are not final for the full fiscal year.",
